# Favor stateless event-driven design

Prefer **stateless, event-driven** flows. Keeping history/state should be the **exception**, not the default.

## Prefer

- Arm once from a valid discovery/hit event (`RegisterForRemoteEvent`, `RegisterForHitEvent`, `RegisterForKey`, timers that only re-arm).
- Decide eligibility **when arming** (e.g. `IsValidTarget` on `RegisterTarget`), then settle on the event (`OnDeath`, `OnHit`, sleep stop) with **thin** gates (blade drawn, killer==player, cooldown) — do not rebuild identity/hostility history at settle time.
- Prefer the engine registration itself over FormID “seen while friendly” lists. Leave-range cleanup (`UnRegisterTarget`) should still clear what it armed (`OnDeath`, hits) — do not invent sticky leave-range state to paper over missed arms.
- Fail loud with `Debug.Trace` / status when an event path bails.

## Avoid (unless explicitly justified)

- Parallel FormID / Actor arrays that mirror “we saw them once” for a check the event registration already encodes.
- Re-running hard gates (`IsValidTarget`, hostility) on the kill / settle call chain after a prior valid arm.
- New session-long tracking lists “just in case” when a remote event or alias can own the lifetime.

## When state is justified

State is OK when the engine cannot express the rule as an event (caps, FIFO registries, MCM latches, temp essential tracking you must reverse, decay clocks). Document **why** the list exists and what cleans it up.

## Example

```papyrus
; BAD — history list + re-check at death
NoteFriendlySeen(ak) ; ambient
; ...
If !WasFriendlySeen(victim) || !IsValidTarget(victim)
	Return ; settler who aggro'd fails
EndIf

; GOOD — arm while valid; settle without re-checking identity/hostility
If IsValidTarget(akTarget)
	RegisterForRemoteEvent(akTarget, "OnDeath")
EndIf
; UnRegisterTarget: clear OnDeath + hits (leave-range cleanup)
; OnDeath / RewardKill: blade + player killer only — no IsValidTarget
; (In-range after aggro: prior arm remains until UnRegisterTarget; do not re-gate settle)
```
